Z||000011||frontal lobe||07-21-2000||01:15 AM||||Yea, Hugh.  No problem singing like the celebrities during the national anthem.  Really, no offense at all, but if you can't sing the national anthem well and MUST sing it, well, there is always the shower!<P>Hey, let me rant on a sore subject since it got brought up.  You know, when people sing the national anthem,  it IS NOT SOME REGULAR ENTERTAINER SONG TO SHOW OFF YOUR MUSICAL ABILITIES.  It is an ANTHEM.  The focus is supposed to be directed at THE WORDS, not the singer's phenomenal ability.  Don't get me wrong, I'm NOT against doing it well.  Just make the center of attention FOR JUST THAT ONE SONG, PLEASE, the meaning and NOT yourself.  There, I got that off my chest.  Thanks for listening.<P>By the way, to our Canadian friends out there, I like the music to the Canadian national anthem better.  That is one fun song to sing.  You guys must love singing along to that one.||||reg||1
